  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fighting Impunity for International Crimes in the Kasais - Figthing Impunity for International Crimes in the Kasais</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">R&#xe4;ttvisa f&#xf6;r internationella brott i Kasaierna</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">TRIAL international har tillsammans med Physicians for Human Rights utvecklat en insats  som syftar till att bek&#xe4;mpa straffriheten f&#xf6;r grova brott mot m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter beg&#xe5;ngna under de senaste &#xe5;ren i Kasai-provinserna, inklusive, men inte uteslutande, s&#xe5;dana beg&#xe5;ngna inom ramen f&#xf6;r dem v&#xe4;pnade konflikten 2016-2017.  Detta innefattar att st&#xe4;rka f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;gan hos akt&#xf6;rer inom, och partners till, det lokala r&#xe4;ttssystemet att utreda, &#xe5;tala och st&#xe4;lla till svars ansvariga. Verksamheten kommer att omfatta utbildning av personal inom  den civila och milit&#xe4;ra r&#xe4;ttskedjan, inklusive &#xe5;klagare, domare, f&#xf6;rsvarare, r&#xe4;ttstekniker, utredande polis, samt NGOs aktiva inom omr&#xe5;dena. Projektet kommer &#xe4;ven att coacha enskilda &#xe4;renden genom r&#xe4;ttssystemet, till st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r brottsoffer och relevanta instanser, f&#xf6;r att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra effektiva och r&#xe4;ttss&#xe4;kra r&#xe4;ttsprocesser, domar och uppf&#xf6;ljning inklusive kompensation till brottsoffer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Partner, TRIAL international, in cooperation with Physicians for Human Rights, has developed this project with the aim to combatting impunity for serious human rights violations committed in recent years in the Kasa&#xef; provinces in the DRC, including, but not limited to, those committed within the context of the armed conflict 2016- 2017. This includes strengthening the capacities of actors within, and partners to, the national judicial and law enforcement authorities to investigate cases, prosecute suspects and bring perpetrators to justice. The activities will include training of civilian and military judicial functions, including prosecutors, judges, defense lawyers, forensic technicians, investigative police, as well as NGOs active in these areas. The project will also coach individual cases through the justice system, supporting victims of crimes and relevant judicial bodies, to enable effective and legal processes in conformity with the rule of law, judgements and compensation to victims of human rights abuses.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of the intervention is to contribute to the fight against impunity and to promote the access to transitional justice in the Kasai region. This is to be done by promoting access to justice to victims of human rights violations and by reinforcing the capacity of the judicial system and other stake holders relevant to reinforcing rule of law and equitable justice principles in the DRC.</narrative>
  </description>
